        {
          "ruleId": "owasp-audit/CVE-2022-24999/package-lock.json/qs",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Needs validation: Express 4.17.1 resolves qs 6.7.0, affected by CVE-2022-24999 (query-string __proto__ process hang), reachable pre-auth. Blockers: Whether the installed qs 6.7.0, called through Express 4.17.1's default extended query parser, blocks the event loop on a[__proto__]b&a[__proto__]&a[length]=100000000. This needs node_modules or npm audit, and both were out of scope here. Validation plan: Locally, from the repo root: `npm ci && npm audit --omit=dev` (look for qs, GHSA for CVE-2022-24999). Then `PORT=3999 node src/app.js &` and run `curl -s -m 5 -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\\n' 'http://localhost:3999/healthz?a[__proto__]b&a[__proto__]&a[length]=100000000'; curl -s -m 5 http://localhost:3999/healthz`. Confirmed: the first curl times out (exit 28) and the plain /healthz also stalls while node sits at 100% CPU. Rejected: both return quickly (200 / 'ok') and npm audit doesn't list qs."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
